  "pathwayDescription": "The Vietnam Energy Outlook Report is a governmental publication, developed by the Electricity and Renewable Energy Authority (EREA) in collaboration with external partners, that provides multiple potential pathways for Vietnam's energy sector. Its Green Growth scenario is a variation of the Net-Zero pathway that focuses on a less energy-intensive economic development trajectory, while still achieving the country's 2050 net-zero target. It assumes a faster shift in GDP contributions away from energy-intensive industries and toward the services sector, while maintaining the same overall GDP growth rate. This means that while the growth in energy demand in Vietnam is still high under this scenario, it is lower than that of other scenarios. In this scenario, the structure of the economy shifts, with industry's share of GDP dropping to 30% (as opposed to 40% in the regular Net Zero case), while services grow to 60% (as opposed to 50%). Other than this shift, the Green Growth scenario does not introduce new climate policies or technology cost changes beyond the Net Zero scenario, and any differences are due to the changes in economic composition.",
